\paragraph{Why interventions fail; practical implications.}
\label{sec:detector}
\looseness=-1 CIVO is an emergent property of co-adapting embeddings, not a single-pathway defect: SGS fails from pathway redundancy; RAVE fails as the EMA anchor tracks biased values; TCN shows binary behavior suggesting a phase transition. Wide dual-critic achieves prevention in 3/4 seeds (NVE $\leq 1.4\times$), though cross-environment transfer is limited. These findings generalize beyond DreamerV3: embedding co-adaptation may interact pathologically with value estimation in any imagination-based actor-critic that bootstraps within a learned model. Practitioners should: (1)~monitor NVE throughout training ($\geq 2.0\times$ indicates onset; Algorithm~\ref{alg:civo_detector}, Appendix~\ref{sec:detector_appendix}); (2)~use frozen-embedding runs as diagnostic controls; (3)~prefer MPC-style re-planning for variable-rate execution.

